# Adjacent bracket groups `a[1][0]` are the flat rectangular index of ONE Array by the strides its description knows (the
# book: semantics "fields" 116 and "arrays" 1030, L2 spec 284, CORE 5.2; Codex CODEX-ARRAY-GROUPS-20261011-184637); they never
# select the inner Array of an Array of Arrays -- that is `a[1]\[0]`.  Rectangular construction is not built, so the flat
# form is refused at its second group, in both modes (steps/defects.md FLAT-INDEX-READ-AS-NESTED).
fn: work () int
    []: []: int a 2
    []: int row 3
    a[1]: row
    row[0]: 5
    if: a[1][0] != 5
        return: 81
    return: 7
end: work
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: work(); stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
